{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179400-help-on-a-storyline","id":1179400,"title":"Help on a storyline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-25T19:35:14-08:00","id":1179400,"title":"Help on a storyline","content":"I am currently running my first Werewolf chronicle, which is set in New Orleans. Currently, my PCs are in their Rite of Passage, which is tracking where Wyrm Tainted Moonshine is coming from and destroying the manufacturers of it. I am currently planning out the final phases of it. But, this is not the storyline i need help on. After my PCs get their spirit totem from the Umbra, i am planning on introducing the PCs to a multi-national corporation based in India called Singh Telecommunications, a corporation that serves the Weaver. The way they get introduced is through the Chairman's son, Rajit, who is a party animal on vacation in New Orleans to sow his wild oats. Basically, a Glass Walker who wants to talk to Rajit's father tasks the PCs with convincing Rajit to make his Father accept his invitation. But, through a series of events, they end up pissing Rajit's Father to the point where he attempts to have the PCs killed.<br /> <br /> This is where i am so far with this storyline. Can i have some advice on how to make Singh Telecommunications a threat to the PCs and can i have some input on why the Glass Walker would want to talk to a Weaver servant and what the PCs could do to piss off Mr. Singh, Rajit's father?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:30:52-08:00","id":1179592,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you have a very particular event in mind that requires a lot of things to go right. I suggest you step back and come up with a more general event/situation that allows more PC agency, and that will create several different kind of consequences depending on PC actions. If the PCs don't do something that results in a fight, what will happen instead? You should allow that to be explored while still keeping the potential for violence in later actions. Don't make this too scripted.<br /> <br /> This is how I would develop your scenario.<br /> <br /> First, you need an answer as to <i>how</i> a telecommunications company serves the Weaver. One possibility is that as part of their advanced wireless program, they somehow began receiving or perhaps intercepting &quot;transmissions&quot; from an unknown source, but definitely higher intelligence. (This source is probably some extremely powerful Net-Spider jaggling or equivalent, but perhaps it is also some kind of Weaver spirit Incarna depending on whether you want the PCs to ultimately encounter and defeat it). The transmissions, once decoded, was a form of higher mathematics which showed extremely advanced algorithims which allows for all sorts of super security encryption/decryption. Thus Singh Telecommunications became a world leader in telecommunications security. All sorts of people want that technology.<br /> <br /> Second, this is why the Glass Walker wants to talk with the Chairman. He wants that technology as well. He's discovered not even GW theurges and their spirit allies have been able to hack it. So he's interested in learning more. Perhaps at this time, he doesn't even realize the extent of the Weaver's involvement. Although he may suspect some thing. Furthermore, the PCs can quickly discover that the spread of this technology can threaten any Garou's control of technology to whatever extent you want the threat to be. One or more of the below may already be true, or introduced during the chronicle to ratchet up the threat. The Weaver spirits found near them are more powerful than normal and incredibly aggressive. Web domains quickly sprout up around STC's networks. New kind of Weaver spirits are being identified, and when they encounter Garou friendly spirits in tech (that have allowed GW's secure communications, super hacking abilities, etc.) they destroy them. Even some Gifts don't seem to work on these devices - Jam Technology, Gremlins, Cybersenses, Control Complex Machine, Signal Rider, etc. just don't work - or require increasing difficulties to do so. Furthermore, it is suspected that someone or something is now collecting information of existing GW networks and information leading to a massive security breach.<br /> <br /> Third, needless to say, the &quot;transmissions&quot; are an important trade secret to Singh Telecommunications. Without it, they have no competitive advantage in an extremely competitive field that is always changing. They don't understand the source of the transmissions. Is it extra-terrestrial? Extra-dimensional? Dark matter? Something or someone more mundane? Their attempts at contact have had mild and uncertain success. Only one piece of expensive R&amp;D prototype is able to receive the transmissions, and attempts to upgrade it sometimes causes the transmissions to cease. Only a small R&amp;D team and the Chairman know the source of their discoveries, and they publicly attribute their work to a very specific and secret skunkworks project. All the members do though is record the tranmissions, decode them, and see what happens when they try to use that knowledge. Since vast fortunes are at stake, the Chairman will do anything to protect this source and their exclusive access to it.<br /> <br /> Fourth, each subsequent transmission reveals more and more information. Think of how the alien intelligence communicated to people in the movies Contact and Species. The transmissions are now revealing actual technology and genetic engineering and advanced physics which generates even more engineering possibilities. This is where you can justify actual strange WeaverTech or cybernetic &quot;upgrades&quot; to normal humans and animals. This is how you can explain super powered killers to throw at the PCs if you want, or you can keep this more mundane.<br /> <br /> So once the PCs intercept Rajit and begin to make inquiries, all sorts of red flags are raised. Who are these people? What do they want? Do they intend to steal his secrets? Might they learn about the transmissions? Perhaps the Chairman knows that someone has been attempting to crack into his system (the GW). His security measures have even traced that this GW is behind these attempts, and once he's linked the PCs to them, they are an obvious threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}